Third-party components
======================

This repository vendors no third-party source. Every dependency is fetched by
CMake at configure time and stays under its own licence.

fortfem (lazy-fortran/fortfem) -- MIT
    Only the dependency-free triangle_compat mesher is built.

Delaunay32 (morishuz/delaunay32) -- MIT
    Header/library for constrained Delaunay on quantised integer coordinates.

fortplot (lazy-fortran/fortplot) -- MIT
    Plotting.

Triangle (J. R. Shewchuk), fetched from salsa.debian.org/science-team/triangle
    NOT free software and NOT covered by this repository's MIT licence.
    Its terms permit redistribution only if no compensation is received, and
    distribution as part of a commercial system requires a direct arrangement
    with the author. Debian ships it in non-free.

    The Triangle backend is therefore opt-in (-DBENCH_WITH_TRIANGLE=ON) and
    builds a local copy for comparison only. Do not redistribute the resulting
    binaries.

The reference meshes under cases/*/reference/ are output data produced by
Triangle from our own boundary inputs. They are covered by this repository's
MIT licence; the Triangle source that produced them is not distributed here.

The boundary inputs under cases/*/boundary.dat come from MEPHIT
(github.com/itpplasma/MEPHIT, MIT) run on the synthetic circular test
equilibrium shipped with it. They contain no experimental machine data.
